      "worked": "With $\\theta$ in radians, the sector area is $\\frac12r^2\\theta$ and the area of triangle $OAB$ is $\\frac12r^2\\sin\\theta$. The triangle occupies half the sector area, so\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac12r^2\\sin\\theta&=\\frac12\\left(\\frac12r^2\\theta\\right)\\\\\\sin\\theta&=\\frac{\\theta}{2}.\\end{align*}$$\nFrom the graph in question 40, the positive solution satisfies $\\frac{\\pi}{2}<\\theta<\\pi$. Hence $\\theta$ is obtuse.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
